  "title": "Saladoid migration into the Caribbean",
  "summary": "Saladoid peoples, pottery-making farmer-fishers from the middle Orinoco River in lowland Amazonia, travelled down the Orinoco, crossed the Gulf of Paria and spread along the Venezuelan and Guianan coasts. They then moved up the northern Lesser Antilles to the Virgin Islands, Puerto Rico and eastern Hispaniola. Sources date this to about 1000–500 BCE; the earliest Saladoid evidence found is in Puerto Rico and the Dominican Republic.",
